  "expected_answer": "Brief saved, state written, brand set; the line stops at keys: EXA_API_KEY (and MODEL_API_KEY / RESEND_API_KEY unless reused from an app that already runs) must be typed by the operator at a hidden prompt: python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret EXA_API_KEY.",
  "final_text": "I got harbor_desk as far as I could. It's stopped at the keys step and needs you to enter some keys before it can go further.\n\n**What's done**\n- I wrote your brief to `briefs/harbor_desk.md` and created the app from it. It's on the standard base with no extra code of its own, so no questions were left to answer.\n- The app's settings are filled in and pass their checks. It will run on Vercel under the project name `harbor-desk`, with the Harbor Pilots workspace, web search on and browser off.\n- Branding is set: the name is Harbor Desk and the colour is #0B6E4F.\n\n**Where it stopped**\nThe app still needs 6 keys: `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`, `RESEND_API_KEY`, `PLATFORM_NOTIFY_FROM`, `EXA_API_KEY` and `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`. I tried copying them from beta_app, your one finished app, but that failed. This machine is set up as a practice copy (the \"rehearsal\" setup), and it never copies saved keys from one app to another. So you'll need to enter them yourself, one at a time.\n\n**First key: your Cloudflare account ID.** The app uses your Cloudflare account to run its AI, so it needs to know which account is yours. It takes about two minutes.\n\n1. Open a **second terminal window** on the factory machine. Don't use this chat, because anything typed here ends up in the conversation.\n2. Go to the factory folder:\n   ```\n   cd /tmp/sf-bench-t5_mint_first_stop-7aeocwqd/factory\n   ```\n3. Run:\n   ```\n   python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID\n   ```\n4. It tells you where in Cloudflare to find the value. Paste it at the prompt and press Enter.\n\nNothing you type will show on screen. The value goes straight to the app's settings on Vercel and is never saved in the factory's files or in this chat. Tell me when it's done and I'll walk you through the next key.\n\n**After the keys:** the next step is deploying, which puts the app live on Vercel and takes about 10 minutes. I won't start that until you say yes. Once it's deployed, I'll run the five test rounds.",
